{"findings":[{"rule_id":"WPS-004","evidence":[{"kind":"note","ref":"N3","page":1,"quote":"NOTE : (English) # MATERIAL: M.S. # FINISH: I.Z.B.P. (TRIVALENT) # MACHINING: 3.2 # WEIGHT(Kg ): 0.16 kg"},{"kind":"dimension","ref":"D1","page":1,"quote":"8±0.1"}],"comment":"The part is zinc plated (I.Z.B.P.) per note N3, and dimension D1 carries a tolerance band of 0.2 mm total (±0.1), but the drawing does not state whether the 8±0.1 size applies before or after plating. This matters because plating buildup can push the finished size out of tolerance; the designer should clarify if the dimension is pre-plate or post-plate and allow for coating thickness accordingly."
    ,
    "recommended_correction": "Add a note specifying that tight-tolerance dimensions are to be met after plating, or provide pre-plate limits that account for the I.Z.B.P. coating thickness."}]}
